@startuml UC13_Change_Authentication_Details_Sequence_Diagram

title UC13: Change Authentication Details - Sequence Diagram

actor "End User" as User
participant "Frontend" as Frontend
participant "Authentication Service\n(Firebase Auth)" as Auth

note over User, Auth
  Precondition: user is logged in. Entirely a
  Frontend-to-Authentication-Service interaction -
  the User Actions Server plays no part in it, and
  nothing is stored locally (same as UC1/UC14).
end note

User -> Frontend: Select "Account Settings"

alt E1: Authentication Service unavailable
  Frontend -> User: Display error,\nallow retry later
  note right: Flow ends (E1)
else Authentication Service available
  Frontend -> User: Display editable username/email/\npassword fields, pre-filled from\ncurrent Firebase user object
  User -> Frontend: Update one or more fields,\nconfirm

  Frontend -> Auth: Call SDK method (updateProfile /\nupdateEmail / updatePassword)

  alt A1: Re-authentication required
    Auth --> Frontend: Rejected - session not\nrecent enough
    Frontend -> User: Prompt to re-enter password
    User -> Frontend: Enter password
    Frontend -> Auth: Re-authenticate\n(SDK re-auth method)
    Auth --> Frontend: Re-authenticated
    Frontend -> Auth: Retry the change\n(same SDK method)
    Auth --> Frontend: Change validated and applied
  else Session recent enough
    Auth --> Frontend: Change validated and applied
  end

  Frontend -> User: Display confirmation message
end

@enduml
